{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The capability map can DECLARE the Epic fields absent when no Software project existed\n\nFound by the parity sweep while fixing [rebar:9790-cafa-dffa-462e]. **The ticket's original\nprescribed fix (a pre-run `await_required_fields` call) is REFUTED** — see the triage comment: that\npre-create call site is exactly what bug 941b-f049-5f29-4410 landed to remove, and\n`scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` bans it in terms. `main()` creates no Jira Software project\nbefore the agent run, so a pre-run wait would burn its whole budget and abort every run.\n\n**Operator decision 2026-08-12: option (a) — post-run validation only.** No pre-create wait, no\nthrowaway project, no prompt changes.\n\n## The real defect\n\n`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:main()` writes `capability_map.json` and returns 0 for ANY\nstructured answer the agent returns. If the agent read `/rest/api/2/field` before creating its first\nSoftware project, it sees 27 system fields and zero `customfield_*` entries (run 30981084637), and\ncan legitimately report `epic_link_field_id=None` / `epic_name_field_id=None`. That report is the\nauthority a human uses to update `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` / `_PROJECT_TEMPLATE` in\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py`. Nothing today makes the reader notice.\n\n## Fix (option a)\n\nAfter the run returns, apply the 941b discriminator to the recorded evidence:\n\n- If the answer reports **either** Epic field id as null **and** the last usable\n  `GET /rest/api/2/field` captured in `_EVIDENCE` carries **zero** `customfield_*` ids (including the\n  case where no usable field read was captured at all), the \"absent\" claim is **not verifiable** —\n  it is indistinguishable from \"no Jira Software project existed yet\".\n- In that case mark the report UNVERIFIED and fail the job (non-zero exit), quoting both candidate\n  causes and the observed inventory. `capability_map.json` and `evidence.json` are still written, so\n  the human keeps the artifact — they just cannot mistake it for a verified contract.\n- Any other combination (fields reported present, or absent while other `customfield_*` ids exist)\n  is untouched: exit code and artifacts are exactly as today.\n\nThe `customfield_*` count is a small pure helper added to `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py`\n(stdlib-only, the module of record for this discriminator); the validation itself is a pure function\nin the capability-map script so a unit test can drive it without Jira or an LLM.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` exposes a pure validation function that, given a structured\n      answer plus the recorded REST evidence, returns an UNVERIFIED reason exactly when the answer\n      reports an Epic field id as null AND the recorded field inventory holds zero `customfield_*`\n      ids (or no usable field read at all), and returns \"no problem\" otherwise\n- [ ] `main()` calls it after the agent run: on an UNVERIFIED verdict it prints a `::error::` naming\n      both 941b candidate causes plus the observed inventory, records the verdict in\n      `run_metadata.json`, and returns a non-zero exit code — while still writing\n      `capability_map.json` and `evidence.json`\n- [ ] `main()` behaviour is unchanged for every other answer shape (Epic fields present, or absent\n      alongside other `customfield_*` ids): same exit code and same artifacts as before this change\n- [ ] no pre-create `await_required_fields` call is added anywhere (the 941b ban holds), and a test\n      pins that `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` contains no such call site\n- [ ] unit tests drive the validator with: a system-only inventory + null Epic ids (UNVERIFIED), a\n      provisioned inventory + null Epic ids (accepted — genuine degrade), populated Epic ids (accepted),\n      and no field read captured (UNVERIFIED)\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py -q\n    make lint && make typecheck","title":"Capability map declares Epic fields absent without validating the report against the recorded field inventory"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786516621055535001,"uuid":"18109366-8417-413d-85dd-1640c71985bf"}